<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>__kp_Location is assigned by the server. A row created here takes a</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>negative key instead: the server only ever issues positives, so a local</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>key can never collide with a real one, and any negative value reads as</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>'not uploaded yet'. UploadChanges swaps in the real key and repoints the</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>location's equipment straight after the create.</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>Assigned here rather than by an auto-enter serial because FileMaker</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="89" name="# (comment)"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Restore state="False"/><Text>serials cannot count down -- the increment must be positive.</Text></Step>
<Step enable="True" id="141" name="Set Variable"><DisableStepCollapsed state="False"/><Value><Calculation><![CDATA[Let ( m = GetAsNumber ( ExecuteSQL ( "select min ( \"__kp_Location\" ) from \"Locations\" where \"__kp_Location\" < 0" ; "" ; "" ) ) ; If ( m < 0 ; m - 1 ; -1 ) )]]></Calculation></Value><Repetition><Calculation><![CDATA[1]]></Calculation></Repetition><Name>$localKey</Name></Step>
